<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Telesp H1 net climbs vs yr ago.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Telesp H1 net climbs vs yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Telecomunicacoes de Sao Paulo  SA (Telesp), a unit of federal telecom holding Telebras serving Sao  Paulo state, on Friday released the following preliminary financial  results for the first six months of 1997:</p>
<p>		Jan-June 1997	    Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>Net	     447.9 million	    391.4 million</p>
<p>Shr Net	 8.43			 7.36</p>
<p>Net Revs	2.076 billion	    1.682 billion</p>
<p>Oper Net	672.5 million	    497.7 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures are in Brazilian reais and not adjusted for inflation.  Share net is per lot of 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>The company reported a first-half net worth of 9.753 billion reais  compared with 9.468 billion at the end of the first quarter.</p>
<p>((-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
</text>
